<p><small>Guide updated 30 September 2026. Property availability and commercial terms change; use the current vacancy schedule for individual opportunities.</small></p>
<h2 id="choose-your-space">Which type of space fits your business?</h2>
<p>A business park in Midrand can bring office teams, customer-facing functions and operational space into one location. The useful starting point is the work you need the premises to support: a dedicated head office, a furnished base for a small team, a warehouse, or offices connected to an operational floor.</p>
<p>At Midpoint, you can compare conventional offices, OnPoint serviced offices and warehouse opportunities within the same estate. Start with the options below, then check the size, asking rental, occupation date and specifications of the individual space.</p>
<div role="region" aria-label="Compare workspace types" tabindex="0" style="overflow-x:auto">
<table>
<caption>Three ways to occupy space at Midpoint</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Space</th><th scope="col">Consider it when</th><th scope="col">Compare before choosing</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row"><a href="/offices">Conventional offices</a></th><td>Your team needs dedicated premises, its own reception or control over layout and branding.</td><td>Usable layout, fit-out condition, meeting rooms, parking and the full monthly cost.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row"><a href="/services-offices">OnPoint serviced offices</a></th><td>You need a furnished workspace for a smaller team, project or satellite operation.</td><td>Suite capacity, agreed term, included services, meeting-room access and additional charges.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row"><a href="/warehouses">Warehouses and integrated offices</a></th><td>Stock, deliveries, distribution or other permitted operations need space alongside administration.</td><td>Clear height, office proportion, loading, yard circulation, power and suitability for your intended use.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href="/vacancies">View current Midpoint vacancies, sizes and asking rentals</a>, or <a href="/contact-us">send the leasing team your requirements</a>. A published opportunity may need a notice period or building works before occupation; available to enquire about does not always mean ready to move into today.</p>

<h2 id="midrand-location">Halfway House, Midrand: assess the complete journey</h2>
<p>Midpoint is at <strong>162 Tonetti Street, Halfway House, Midrand, 1685</strong>, alongside the N1 on the Johannesburg–Pretoria corridor. This location is worth considering when staff, clients or suppliers travel from different parts of Gauteng and the business needs a base between the two cities.</p>
<p>Highway frontage and the route to a building are different things. Before a viewing, confirm the correct visitor or delivery entrance with the leasing team. Test the journey from the interchange to that entrance and from the gate to the specific office or loading area.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>For office teams:</strong> compare representative staff journeys at arrival and departure times, visitor parking and the walk from parking to reception.</li>
<li><strong>For public-transport users:</strong> check the complete connection from the relevant station or stop to the estate, including the last leg and the return journey. Do not assume a Gautrain shuttle, walking route or late-shift service is available.</li>
<li><strong>For deliveries:</strong> confirm the permitted vehicle route, gate dimensions, turning area, queueing space and receiving hours for the shortlisted building.</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="/location">Explore Midpoint location and access</a>. Arrange a viewing at a time that reflects how your business will operate.</p>

<h3>Comparing Midrand business parks and nearby commercial nodes</h3>
<p>If your shortlist includes Halfway House, Waterfall, Kyalami, other Midrand locations, Sandton or Centurion, compare actual buildings against the same brief. A suburb name alone cannot establish a better commute, lower cost or suitable specification.</p>
<p>Record the journeys that happen most often, then compare usable space, parking, occupation date and total cost. A business combining offices and stock handling should also compare the cost and travel involved in splitting those activities across separate premises. Midpoint is one estate option in that exercise; a business whose essential journeys cluster elsewhere may find another location more practical.</p>

<h2 id="leasing-costs">What does it cost to rent space in a Midrand business park?</h2>
<p>The answer depends on the unit and what its quotation includes. Ask for the monthly rental as well as the rate per square metre, and establish whether the quoted area includes an office component or other space. Treat an advertised asking rate as the start of a comparison, not the complete occupation budget.</p>
<p>For a conventional lease, separate these costs:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Rental:</strong> quoted lettable area multiplied by the agreed rental rate, with any separately priced areas identified.</li>
<li><strong>Recurring extras:</strong> operating costs or recoveries, parking, metered utilities, connectivity and any separately charged services.</li>
<li><strong>Once-off costs and upfront cash:</strong> deposit, moving, fit-out, furniture, racking, signage and installation charges. A refundable deposit is cash tied up, not the same as a monthly expense.</li>
<li><strong>Costs over the term:</strong> escalation, maintenance responsibilities, agreed reinstatement and any incentives or landlord contributions.</li>
</ul>
<p>Ask which amounts include VAT and which exclude it. Check what a serviced-office package includes before comparing it with an unfurnished conventional office, and avoid counting a service twice if it is already included in the quoted rental.</p>

<h3>A worked example: why the lowest rate may cost more</h3>
<p><strong>Illustration only:</strong> these invented figures explain the calculation. They are not Midpoint quotations, available units or Midrand market averages. Both examples assume 500 m² and 10 parking bays; all figures exclude VAT.</p>
<div role="region" aria-label="Illustrative monthly occupancy costs" tabindex="0" style="overflow-x:auto">
<table>
<caption>Illustrative monthly comparison for two 500 m² offices</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Monthly item</th><th scope="col">Example A</th><th scope="col">Example B</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Base rental</th><td>500 m² × R100 = R50,000</td><td>500 m² × R90 = R45,000</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Operating costs</th><td>500 m² × R20 = R10,000</td><td>500 m² × R30 = R15,000</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Parking</th><td>10 bays × R500 = R5,000</td><td>10 bays × R750 = R7,500</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Subtotal before other costs</th><td><strong>R65,000 per month</strong></td><td><strong>R67,500 per month</strong></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Example B has a lower base rate but a subtotal R2,500 higher each month. Utilities, connectivity, VAT, deposits and fit-out are excluded from both examples and must still be assessed. Apply the same worksheet to current written quotations, using the same lease period and clearly stated assumptions.</p>
<p><a href="/contact-us">Request a breakdown for your shortlisted Midpoint space</a>. The leasing team can explain the quoted area, included items and occupation requirements for that unit.</p>

<h2 id="building-checklist">A practical business-park viewing checklist</h2>
<p>Take your requirements to the viewing and record an answer for each item below. Mark information still awaiting confirmation so it cannot be mistaken for an agreed building specification.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Layout and capacity.</strong> Test desks, meeting rooms, storage and circulation on an accurate floor plan. For a warehouse, include racking, receiving, picking, dispatch, returns and the office component.</li>
<li><strong>Power and water.</strong> Midpoint has generator-backed power and backup water with N+1 redundancy. Confirm which loads and areas are supported for the specific unit, changeover arrangements, metering and charges. These estate provisions do not establish that every piece of tenant equipment is covered.</li>
<li><strong>Connectivity.</strong> Confirm providers, installation lead times and redundancy options for the building. Check practical mobile reception where staff and equipment will be working.</li>
<li><strong>Access and parking.</strong> Record allocated staff and visitor bays, additional-bay charges, accessibility, delivery procedures and after-hours arrangements. Confirm security responsibilities at estate and unit level.</li>
<li><strong>Warehouse specification.</strong> Measure clear height to the lowest obstruction, door openings and yard dimensions. Check vehicle movements and the suitability of the floor, fire systems and permitted use with the relevant specialists.</li>
<li><strong>Condition and timing.</strong> Agree the handover condition, works required, responsibility for costs and a realistic occupation programme. Distinguish an existing fitted space from a proposed conversion or future development.</li>
<li><strong>Commercial terms.</strong> Compare the written rental breakdown, deposit, term, escalation, fit-out contribution and maintenance obligations. Have the final lease and technical requirements reviewed by the appropriate advisers.</li>
</ol>
<p>For more detail, use the <a href="/offices">office leasing guide</a> or <a href="/warehouses">warehouse specification and shortlisting guide</a>. These help turn a general estate shortlist into a building-specific brief.</p>

<h2 id="working-at-midpoint">Amenities, working life and room to grow</h2>
<p>Midpoint brings workspace together with food, fitness and outdoor facilities. The estate offering includes Fond restaurant and bar, cafés, gym and padel facilities, and walking, running and cycling trails. Check current opening hours, access arrangements and charges for the facilities your team intends to use.</p>
<p><strong>The Suites at Midpoint is coming soon.</strong> Corporate accommodation should not be treated as an operating facility when planning a move or arranging visiting teams. Its published renderings illustrate the proposed accommodation; final finishes may differ.</p>
<p><a href="/amenities">Explore the estate amenities and their current or planned status</a>. During a viewing, walk the route from the proposed premises to the facilities that matter to your team rather than assuming every building has the same proximity.</p>
<p>Having serviced offices, conventional offices and warehouses in one estate can make it easier to discuss changing requirements with one leasing team. Moving to a larger unit, adding adjacent space or changing workspace type remains subject to availability, suitability and agreed terms; it is not an automatic expansion right.</p>

<h2 id="leasing-process">From first enquiry to occupation</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Send a usable brief.</strong> Include the preferred move date, area range, headcount, parking, budget and intended use. Warehouse briefs should also specify vehicle types, loading, power and office requirements.</li>
<li><strong>Shortlist current opportunities.</strong> Review the vacancy schedule, request floor plans and clarify availability dates. Brokers representing tenants can use the same schedule and contact the leasing team with a brief.</li>
<li><strong>View and resolve the unknowns.</strong> Bring the people responsible for operations, IT or workplace planning where relevant. Record outstanding specifications and landlord or tenant works.</li>
<li><strong>Agree the premises and programme.</strong> Confirm the commercial terms, approvals, handover condition and occupation arrangements in the final documentation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Midpoint is owned and developed by <a href="https://www.blendproperty.co.za/">Blend Property Group</a>, which has specialised in commercial and industrial property since 2006. For an enquiry about the estate or a particular building, contact the Midpoint leasing team directly.</p>
<p><strong>Ready to compare actual spaces?</strong> <a href="/vacancies">Browse current vacancies</a> or <a href="/contact-us">book a viewing with the Midpoint leasing team</a>. Share your preferred move date and the requirements that would rule a property in or out.</p>
<p><small>About this guide: estate information is drawn from Midpoint's published location, workspace and amenities pages and Blend Property Group's company information. This is an estate leasing guide, not a survey of the whole Midrand market. Unit specifications, prices, availability and operating arrangements require confirmation for the selected premises.</small></p>
